@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/allotment#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/orexis/market#> .

<> a orexis:SelfGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO THIS AGENT IS: the supplier, and this document is its own by the self it states. Booted as
#  "supplier", the agent checks that this is so; booted as any other, this is not its document.
#
#  WHAT IT RUNS: the market's host, in the market's word — beneath the planner, the executor, the
#  speaker and the deliberator, which the boot loads for it. Its own word about itself, here and never
#  in the public world: a peer finds the host by `market:hosts`, which the society states, and learns
#  nothing of what the host runs.

:supplier a orexis:Self , market:Host .
